meta {
  name: Extract Receipt Text
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/receipts/extract
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "rawInput": "セブン-イレブン 目黒駅東口店\n2026年10月24日 08:42\n※手巻おにぎり 熟成紅しゃけ ¥189\n※サントリー 伊右衛門 600ml ¥160\nレジ袋 ¥3\n合計 ¥352\n(内消費税等 8%対象 ¥25)\n(内消費税等 10%対象 ¥0)\nお預り ¥500\nお釣り ¥148",
    "testcaseId": "{{testcaseId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  POST /api/v1/receipts/extract — text path.

  rawInput is the receipt's plain text exactly as printed (or as OCR
  produced it): newline-separated lines, Japanese, ¥ amounts, footer
  noise like お預り/お釣り. Do not pre-clean or translate — the model
  and the judges are graded on the mess.

  PII (card numbers, 会員番号, TEL) may be included freely: the
  guardrail.pii_redact span scrubs it before the model sees it.

  Response carries X-Trace-Id / X-Span-Id headers — paste the trace id
  into Phoenix (http://localhost:6006) to inspect the extraction.
}
